# H5-OmniFusion Deployment Walkthrough

## 🚀 Current Status: DELETED (Zero Cost / Project Complete)
The system was fully operational (v10) and successfully backed up.
Resources have been targeted for **TOTAL DELETION** to drop costs to absolute $0.
To resume the project in the future, follow the *Disaster Recovery* steps in [azure_deployment_setup.md](file:///c:/Users/thela/OneDrive/Desktop/phase%202/azure_deployment_setup.md).

### 🔗 Architecture
- **Frontend**: Azure Static Web App
- **Backend**: Azure Container App (v10)
  - **Fusion Model**: Baked into Docker image (134MB)
  - **Feature Extraction**: HuggingFace Inference API

### 🌐 Live URLs
| Service | URL | Status | Permanence |
|---------|-----|--------|------------|
| **Frontend** | [Launch App](https://blue-mushroom-094076100.1.azurestaticapps.net) | ✅ Live | **Permanent** |
| **Backend API** | [API Docs](https://h5-backend.bravepebble-1b927c90.southeastasia.azurecontainerapps.io/docs) | ✅ Live (Fusion Ready) | **Permanent** |

### 🛠️ Recent Fixes (v10)
- Fixed `ImportError: H5Config` by using correct [Config](file:///c:/Users/thela/OneDrive/Desktop/phase%202/ml_pipeline/h5_omnifusion/src/config.py#10-288) class.
- Fixed `weights_only=False` for checkpoint loading.
- Fixed dimension mismatches (`d_model=256`, `expert_hidden=128`, `n_quality=5`, `expand=1`).

### 📝 Notes
- **Backend URL**: The `bravepebble` suffix is unique to your Azure environment. It persists across redeployments and updates.
- **Frontend URL**: The `blue-mushroom` name is unique to your Static Web App. It persists indefinitely.
